.TH DIFFALLA-VERIFY 1 "November 2025" "diffalla 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffalla\-verify \- verify a directory matches a snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffalla verify
\fIDIRECTORY\fR \fISNAPSHOT\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verifies that a directory matches a previously created snapshot. This is useful for:
.IP \(bu 2
Integrity monitoring (detect unauthorized changes)
.IP \(bu 2
Build verification (ensure build output matches expected)
.IP \(bu 2
Deployment validation (confirm deployment succeeded)
.IP \(bu 2
Change detection (detect any modifications)
.PP
The command creates a temporary snapshot of the directory and compares it to the reference snapshot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-show\-diff
Show detailed differences if verification fails (lists added/removed/modified files)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Basic verification:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla verify /etc baseline.db
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify with detailed output on failure:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla verify /var/www production\-baseline.db \-\-show\-diff
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use in scripts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
if diffalla verify /critical/dir baseline.db; then
  echo "Directory unchanged"
else
  echo "Changes detected!"
  exit 1
fi
.fi
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
.PP
Success (no changes):
.RS
.nf
✓ Verification successful
  Directory matches snapshot perfectly
.fi
.RE
.PP
Failure (changes detected):
.RS
.nf
✗ Verification failed

Differences:
  Added:    3 files
  Removed:  1 files
  Modified: 2 files
.fi
.RE
.PP
With \-\-show\-diff:
.RS
.nf
Added files:
  + new\-file.txt
  + subdir/another.txt

Removed files:
  \- deleted.txt

Modified files:
  * changed.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Verification successful (directory matches snapshot)
.TP
.B 1
Verification failed (differences found)
.TP
.B 2
Usage error
.TP
.B 3
File system error (directory or snapshot not found)
.SH USE CASES
.SS Integrity Monitoring
Create baseline snapshot of critical directories:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla snapshot /etc \-o /root/etc\-baseline.db
.fi
.RE
.PP
Periodically verify (e.g., via cron):
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla verify /etc /root/etc\-baseline.db || \\
  mail \-s "System changes detected" admin@example.com
.fi
.RE
.SS Build Verification
Capture expected build output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla snapshot /build/expected \-o expected\-output.db
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify actual build:
.PP
.RS
.nf
make build
diffalla verify /build/actual expected\-output.db
.fi
.RE
.SS Deployment Validation
Snapshot production before deployment:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla snapshot /var/www \-o pre\-deploy.db
.fi
.RE
.PP
After deployment, verify expected changes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla verify /var/www expected\-state.db
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
.PP
Temporary snapshot is automatically cleaned up after comparison.
.PP
Only checks file content, metadata, and structure. Does not verify file permissions or ownership unless enabled in snapshot creation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffalla (1),
.BR diffalla\-snapshot (1),
.BR diffalla\-compare (1)
